Finally, you can verify everything using only observable signals (SMTP responses + server logs) by correlating the end-of-`DATA` response line with the presence/absence of the deferral/no-action logs. Enforcement cases (A/C) show end-of-`DATA` `550 5.7.23 SPF authentication failed (msg ID = <id>)` alongside a `smtp: DATA error ... {"check":"apply_spf", ...}` log. The deferral case (B) shows end-of-`DATA` `250 2.0.0 OK: queued` while logs show `apply_spf: deferring action due to a DMARC policy` plus `smtp/pipeline: no check action` (containing the suppressed 550/5.7.23 error fields) and then `smtp: accepted`.

